    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "so that the monotonicity of the operator III may not true in general and depends on the dynamics of the endogenous signal g. The particular case where dgt = g′(t)dt with g′ ≥ 0 (i.e., g is a nondecreasing input curve) and h′ is nonincreasing (i.e., the impact function h is concave on the real line) would yield the monotonicity of III, but such assumptions may be too restrictive."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 552.843, 510.234, 575.508 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Furthermore, verifying the monotonicity property of the operators II and IV in general is not obvious and depends on the form of the kernel G and its first-argument derivative ∂xG."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
